From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:17:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] windows.storage: streamed files are made on first open,
 http(s) sources download

CreateStreamedFileAsync / ReplaceWithStreamedFileAsync now return at once with an
empty file; the application's data-requested handler runs (once) when the file is
first opened or read (OpenAsync/OpenReadAsync, FileIO/PathIO reads, copy, move),
as Windows does. A replaced file keeps its old data until then and when the handler
fails. CreateStreamedFileFromUriAsync / ReplaceWithStreamedFileFromUriAsync with an
http or https URI download through winhttp on first open (an HTTP error status is
HTTP_E_STATUS_*); file:, ms-appx: and ms-appdata: sources are still copied at once.

